static const char _zs216_d[] = "malformed require block\n\nA unit's `require:` block declares what the unit needs from the host toolchain. It must be a unit definition, must declare at least one requirement, and every entry must be a key the compiler consumes -- today only `library:`, whose value is a compile-time string naming a link library. An unknown or misspelt key would be silently ignored, so it is rejected.";
static const z_t84_t _zs216 = { .data = _zs216_d, .size = 384 };
static const char _zs217_d[] = "no main\n\nThe unit being compiled declares no `main: function is { ... }`, so the compiler has no entry point to start from. Compilation is demand-driven: `main` is the root, and what it reaches is what gets checked and emitted. A unit with no `main` is a library -- compile the program that opens it instead, or add a `main`. `--eager` resolves every definition rather than what a root reaches, so it does not require one.";
static const z_t84_t _zs217 = { .data = _zs217_d, .size = 422 };
